Description: Let applications of the desktop use devices of the viewer
 VNC Device Link (https://ps.schlaile.de/tigervnc/spec/): with
 -DeviceLink, Xvnc offers device links to viewers that support them.
 Applications request devices on a control socket in DeviceLinkDir; a
 serial device appears as a pseudo terminal, a tcp or tail device as a
 Unix socket, and the bytes and settings go to the viewer that owns the
 device links (the first one that may use the keyboard). Needs X server
 1.19 for its file descriptor notifications. Backport from
 github.com/schlaile/tigervnc, branch device-link.
Author: Peter Schlaile <peter@schlaile.de>
